descriptionText:
We are seeking an experienced IAM Engineer to assess and modernize our identity and authentication ecosystem. This role will focus on evaluating current Identity Provider (IdP) and Multi-Factor Authentication (MFA) implementations—including Duo, Okta, and Microsoft Entra ID—and designing a strategic roadmap toward a phishing-resistant, passwordless authentication model.&nbsp;
&nbsp;
Key Responsibilities:&nbsp;

- Conduct a comprehensive assessment of existing IdP and MFA solutions (Duo, Okta, Entra ID), including Conditional Access policies and authentication flows&nbsp; 
- Identify gaps, redundancies, and overlapping capabilities across identity platforms&nbsp; 
- Develop a consolidated IAM strategy to reduce tool sprawl, optimize licensing, and lower operational costs&nbsp; 
- Design and implement a roadmap for phishing-resistant, passwordless authentication (e.g., FIDO2/passkeys, device-bound credentials, smartphone-based authenticators)&nbsp; 
- Align identity architecture with Zero Trust principles and organizational security frameworks (e.g., NIST CSF, NIST SP 800-207)&nbsp; 
- Define and enforce Conditional Access policies that support risk-based and adaptive authentication&nbsp; 
- Partner with security, infrastructure, and application teams to integrate modern authentication across SaaS and enterprise systems&nbsp; 
- Provide technical guidance, documentation, and transition planning for migration to the target-state architecture&nbsp;
Qualifications:&nbsp;

- Strong experience with modern IAM platforms (Microsoft Entra ID, Okta, Duo)&nbsp; 
- Deep understanding of MFA, Conditional Access, SSO, federation (SAML/OIDC), and identity lifecycle management&nbsp; 
- Hands-on experience implementing passwordless authentication (FIDO2, passkeys, biometrics)&nbsp; 
- Familiarity with Zero Trust architecture and identity-centric security models&nbsp; 
- Ability to assess complex environments and translate findings into actionable roadmaps&nbsp;
Preferred:&nbsp;

- Experience rationalizing identity platforms and reducing vendor overlap&nbsp; 
- Knowledge of Microsoft 365 E5 security capabilities and integration patterns&nbsp;
Familiarity with NIST standards and enterprise security frameworks&nbsp;
